<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Radimichians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Radimichs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Radimichians were an East Slavic tribe of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, living along the Sozh river in what is now eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>. They paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a> until Oleg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> brought them under his rule in the 880s, and after a rising they were defeated again by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-the-great">Vladimir the Great</a>'s army in 984. Their lands were later divided between the principalities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a>.</p></div>
